From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:30:04 +0900
Subject: Stacking: the input method's panel stays above its layer's other
 windows

The on-screen keyboard is in the overlay layer, as are layer-shell surfaces that ask for it
(Plasma Mobile's panels, a fullscreen view raised above them). One raised after the keyboard
showed covered it: it was there (VirtualKeyboard.visible) but not seen. The input method's
windows now come last in the overlay layer.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic: an overlay surface should not hide the keyboard]
X-Rungic-Tests: none at L3 yet (gap): the fullscreen keyboard on the phone, by hand
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/research/97
Origin: vendor
---
 src/layers.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layers.cpp b/src/layers.cpp
index 29f4086..b36a03a 100644
--- a/src/layers.cpp
+++ b/src/layers.cpp
@@ -585,6 +585,12 @@ QList<Window *> Workspace::constrainedStackingOrder()
         windows[layer] << window;
     }
 
+    // The input method's panel above everything else of its layer: an overlay surface raised later
+    // (a fullscreen view above the shell's panels) must not cover the keyboard it asked for.
+    std::stable_partition(windows[OverlayLayer].begin(), windows[OverlayLayer].end(), [](Window *window) {
+        return !window->isInputMethod();
+    });
+
     QList<Window *> stacking;
     stacking.reserve(unconstrained_stacking_order.count());
     for (uint layer = FirstLayer; layer < NumLayers; ++layer) {
